## DESCRIPTION
## Inverse function theorem
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Inverse function theorem')

########################################################################

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "parserPopUp.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

$mc = PopUp(["?", "Yes", "No"], "Yes");

BEGIN_PGML


Let [` q = (\frac{\pi}{2},\frac{1}{2},0,1) `] and let [` G: \mathbb{R}^4 \to \mathbb{R}^4 `] be given by
>>[` G(w,x,y,z) = \begin{bmatrix} \cos w + wxyz \\ x^2 + y^3 + yz \\ xy + yz + z^5 \\ x^2y + xyz - x^2yz+ 2z \end{bmatrix} `].<<

Is [`G`] a local diffeomorphism at [`q`]? [_]{$mc}
END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();